              "createdAt": "2026-09-25T16:53:38Z",
              "body": "@williammartin I believe this should now be ready for maintainer review :)\r\n\r\nRegarding changes to the prompt about the CONTRIBUTING.md guidelines, I suppose you mean the content of the automated comment, right? I'd suggest including it explicitly in the PR template as well — and if you'd allow me the slight digression, I would also appreciate if the template was written in a way that would make sense if an actual human is filling it out.\r\n\r\nSpecifically, I was a little uncertain in a few aspects, e.g. whether I could omit the \"Key points\" and \"Notes for reviewers\" sections if empty; also, in the \"Authorship and follow-up\" section, the references to @username + \"Name the account\" felt a little awkward and unclear. I ended up adding a note underneath the checklists since none of the options reflected how I used AI for this change."
